      "role": "user",
      "content": "i tried commenting it out and the error stops, so thats definitely that line causing the headache. i also tried running it in a new workbook and it worked perfectly fine there, which is what's driving me crazy. it's like the original file is haunted or something lol. \n\ni've looked through the objects and i cant see anything weird, everything looks normal. is there any way a tiny little piece of junk code or a corrupted cell could just be lurking in there and causing this randomly? it feels like there is some kind of hidden gremlin in the file making it act up.",
      "source": "evaluator"
